"Midas" gets its iconic name from its distinct, all-gold finish. Constructed entirely out of enriched gold-titanium alloy plating, the suit was engineered to withstand high-altitude icing—the exact flaw that almost killed Tony during his flight test in the original Mark II suit in Iron Man. The high concentration of gold prevented thermal locking and ice buildup, allowing the armor to comfortably operate in the upper atmosphere.

In Iron Man 3, Mark XXI flies into action during the House Party Protocol at the Norco oil rig, engaging Extremis forces in air combat before being destroyed in the final "Clean Slate" detonation order.
